      "info": "<meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes' />&nl;<script type='text/javascript'>&nl;const macros = { 'R': 'textsf{R}', 'code': 'texttt'};&nl;function processMathHTML() {&nl;    var l = document.getElementsByClassName('reqn');&nl;    for (let e of l) { katex.render(e.textContent, e, { throwOnError: false, macros }); }&nl;    return;&nl;}</script>&nl;<script defer src='https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.15.3/dist/katex.min.js'&nl;    onload='processMathHTML();'></script>&nl;<table style='width: 100%;'><tr><td>ability.cov</td><td style='text-align: right;'>R Documentation</td></tr></table>&nl;<h2>Ability and Intelligence Tests</h2>&nl;<h3>Description</h3>&nl;<p>Six tests were given to 112 individuals. The covariance matrix is&nl;given in this object.&nl;</p>&nl;<h3>Usage</h3>&nl;<pre><code class='language-R'>ability.cov</code></pre>&nl;<h3>Details</h3>&nl;<p>The tests are described as&nl;</p>&nl;<dl>&nl;<dt>general:</dt><dd><p>a non-verbal measure of general intelligence using&nl;Cattell's culture-fair test.</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;<dt>picture:</dt><dd><p>a picture-completion test</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;<dt>blocks:</dt><dd><p>block design</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;<dt>maze:</dt><dd><p>mazes</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;<dt>reading:</dt><dd><p>reading comprehension</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;<dt>vocab:</dt><dd><p>vocabulary</p>&nl;</dd>&nl;</dl>&nl;<p>Bartholomew gives both covariance and correlation matrices,&nl;but these are inconsistent.  Neither are in the original paper.&nl;</p>&nl;<h3>Source</h3>&nl;<p>Bartholomew, D. J. (1987).&nl;<em>Latent Variable Analysis and Factor Analysis</em>.&nl;Griffin.&nl;</p>&nl;<p>Bartholomew, D. J. and Knott, M. (1990).&nl;<em>Latent Variable Analysis and Factor Analysis</em>.&nl;Second Edition, Arnold.&nl;</p>&nl;<h3>References</h3>&nl;<p>Smith, G. A. and Stanley G. (1983).&nl;Clocking <code class='reqn'>g</code>: relating intelligence and measures of timed&nl;performance.&nl;<em>Intelligence</em>, <b>7</b>, 353&ndash;368.&nl;<a href='https://doi.org/10.1016/0160-2896%2883%2990010-7'>doi:10.1016/0160-2896(83)90010-7</a>.&nl;</p>&nl;<h3>Examples</h3>&nl;<pre><code class='language-R'>&nl;require(stats)&nl;(ability.FA &lt;- factanal(factors = 1, covmat = ability.cov))&nl;update(ability.FA, factors = 2)&nl;## The signs of factors and hence the signs of correlations are&nl;## arbitrary with promax rotation.&nl;update(ability.FA, factors = 2, rotation = 'promax')&nl;</code></pre>&nl;</main>&nl;</div>&nl;",
